# SlugBase

A bookmark manager with built-in URL shortening and keyboard-driven launcher — save bookmarks, assign short slugs, and jump to any URL from the address bar or command palette (`/go/<slug>`). Deployed as a managed hosted service and a self-hosted install from one codebase.

## Tech stack (decisions pending — update as stack is chosen)

- **Single repo:** pnpm workspace monorepo (spec §2.2)
- **Packages:** backend API · web client · shared types/contracts · shared UI · marketing site (static, separately built) · docs (spec §19)
- **Database:** Two engines on identical schema — embedded file-based (self-hosted default) + networked relational (hosted default) — spec §11.9
- **Auth:** Server-side sessions (no JWT access/refresh); TOTP MFA; OIDC/SSO — spec §5
- **Billing:** Stripe (hosted); no-op billing (self-hosted) — spec §11.4
- **i18n:** English + German at launch — spec §17
- **Secrets:** Phase CLI — use the `phase-cli` skill for secrets management
- **Bot protection:** Cloudflare Turnstile (hosted default); no-op (self-hosted) — spec §11.8

